KG42.register("clusters-1dfbd665dfc7a023c0bee221",{"id":"30-motivational_game::v142-d-K003","paper":"30-motivational_game","label":"Mid-market prices and participation incentives under network surplus/deficit scenarios","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K003","label":"Mid-market prices and participation incentives under network surplus/deficit scenarios","market_meaning":"Using grid purchase/sale reference prices, individual surplus/deficit and network surplus/deficit as inputs, peer buy/sell prices are determined according to three scenarios, and satisfying the core requirement through revenue allocation and sustained participation are treated as design requirements. The existing chains provide pricing candidates and participation objectives, but stability verification and behavioral conditions are not yet closed.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["participation","pricing","activation"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The execution scenario of R002 and R006 use the same network surplus/deficit definition from the same coalition case, and quantities are associated only when the participation set, time point and measurement basis are consistent; the roles of execution input and pricing input remain separate. R005-C002 is a prospective description of grid-party influence and is not rewritten as prohibiting CPS trading; price advantage, core stability and psychological participation are distinct claims pending verification.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The same surplus/deficit scenario simultaneously determines CPS surplus trading and the weighted price composition, while pricing is also constrained by the encouragement of participation and the core revenue requirement; together they form a pricing rule cluster with source-text dependencies. R002 only shares the scenario and quantity interfaces, does not reassign its execution rules, and does not infer stability or sustained participation from price bounds.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Bear the price bounds, three-scenario pricing and price-side core revenue requirement, and provide the network surplus/deficit definition and grid-price ordering."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide the requirements that prices should encourage participation and that sustainable operation requires sustained participation; the expectation concerning participant composition retains its original scope."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Only share the individual and network surplus/deficit states and the CPS trading scenarios of C006-C008 as pricing interfaces; no independent execution rules are added."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN008","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::theta_E_n_s","v141-c-R002::theta::theta_E_n_d","v141-c-R002::theta::theta_E_s","v141-c-R002::theta::theta_E_d"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::theta::param_E_ns","v141-c-R006::theta::param_E_nd","v141-c-R006::theta::param_E_s","v141-c-R006::theta::param_E_d"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e18"],"rationale":"The individual surplus/deficit in the same case enters a pricing weighting term, while network surplus/deficit simultaneously selects the execution and pricing scenarios; the specific correspondences are described by four same_quantity mappings, and the local parameters are not merged."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN009","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C006","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C007","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C008"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C005","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e18"],"rationale":"The three source-text scenarios respectively describe simultaneously the CPS trading need and the corresponding pricing, forming complementary responsibilities under the same conditions. Preserve the respective conditions of the balanced, net-surplus and net-deficit branches, and do not treat trading results and price expressions as duplicate constraints."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN010","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005::E::v141-c-R005-E001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e14"],"rationale":"The source text links pricing, the core requirement of revenue allocation and the encouragement of participation, supporting the grouping together of price responsibility and participation requirements; this connection records requirements and the authors' claims, and does not constitute a conclusion that price advantage is sufficient to prove core stability or sustained participation."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM005","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e14"],"rationale":"Both chains' nodes refer to the local pricing function of the same coalition case, and the R006 reference serves as the display representative; the two types of constraints—pricing and participation—and all original objects continue to be retained separately."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM006","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::theta_E_n_s","v141-c-R006::theta::param_E_ns"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e18"],"rationale":"The definition and case formula support the correspondence of the same prosumer surplus, qualified by identical members, time points and measurement basis; the execution-trigger state and the pricing weighting input retain different local roles, and units are not additionally specified."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM007","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::theta_E_n_d","v141-c-R006::theta::param_E_nd"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e18"],"rationale":"The definition and the buyer demand sum in the same case support the correspondence with the individual energy-deficit quantity; retain the two parameters of the energy-purchase branch input and the pricing weighting input, and D does not supplement the specific time scale or units."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM008","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::theta_E_s","v141-c-R006::theta::param_E_s"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e17"],"rationale":"Both use the difference between total surplus and total demand in the same case, associated on the basis of an explicit quantity definition and scenario scope; the execution scenario parameter and the pricing input remain independent originals."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM009","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::theta_E_d","v141-c-R006::theta::param_E_d"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e18"],"rationale":"Both are energy-deficit-side states under the same network surplus/deficit definition, and the source clarifies their sign relationship with network surplus; only the two energy-deficit parameters are associated, surplus and deficit quantities are not merged, and their signed definition is not changed."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-G007","category":"math_incomplete","description":"C002's strict price advantage carries the qualification of actual peer trading; in scenario 2, if total buyer demand is zero, or in scenario 3, if total seller surplus is zero, the weighted unit price will reach the corresponding grid-price endpoint. The existing C has not formalized the effective two-sided transaction domain, the non-negative energy domain, and denominator positivity, so the strict bound cannot be extended to empty-side boundaries.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C005","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C006","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C007","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e10","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e18"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream should clarify the member domains of N_s and N_b, the effective peer transaction conditions, energy non-negativity, and handling of empty sets or zero trading; check the validity of scenario denominators; and preserve the different applicability conditions of the strict advantage and the closed-interval bound."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G008","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The price variable is named peer buy/sell price, but the scenario 2 sell price and scenario 3 buy price contain weighted terms for CPS revenue or cost; it still needs to be clarified whether this is a coalition-level composite effective unit price or a per-transaction peer transaction price, and it cannot be directly inferred as the calculation basis for a single payment amount.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R006::x::var_p_s","v141-c-R006::x::var_p_b","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C005","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e18"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the source text's interpretation of the composite unit price, peer transaction unit price and revenue allocation basis, and have upstream clarify the settlement scope of prices in each scenario; do not rewrite existing variables or formulas, and do not add a mapping from price to payment amount."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G009","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The price-side core requirement lacks the coalition value, revenue allocation vector, core definition and each coalition constraint in frozen C; it is also necessary to distinguish the boundary between the revenue vector belonging to the core and individual revenue. Grid-price comparison and the non-empty core assertion in the source text are insufficient to complete stability verification in the current objects. v141-b-g01-EP01 and v141-b-g02-prop01 remain unapproved.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-a-M01-e13","v141-b-g02-e14"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-EP01","v141-b-g02-prop01"],"required_work":"Upstream must supplement verifiable coalition value, revenue vector and core constraints, and check whether the cited definitions and theorems can support this case and its allocation; after handling the pending proposal, revise C's graph and mathematical binding. D does not substitute a price interval for a stability proof."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G010","category":"ontology_extension","description":"Sustained participation in R005 is a design requirement, not yet a proven behavioral result brought about by the mid-market price. The behavioral stages and five motivational conditions have not formed existing C chains; v141-b-g01-EP04 remains a pending proposal, and the price relationship cannot be equated with a complete psychological participation mechanism.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g03-e002","v141-b-g03-e006"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-EP04"],"required_work":"Upstream must represent the behavioral stages, motivational conditions and their applicable scope separately according to the source text, and handle the pending proposal; retain the authors' judgment of potential, and do not treat economic or environmental performance as a verified causal chain of sustained participation."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G011","category":"unverified_source","description":"The B evidence underlying this cluster's pricing formulas, price advantage, core assertion and participation requirements all remains unverified; this round has no independent source review or scientific endorsement.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11","v141-a-M01-e13","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g03-e002"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the formulas, scenario conditions, price interpretations and cited stability arguments item by item, and manually inspect all quantity correspondences and scope decisions; until then, retain candidate and pending status."}]},"rule_refs":["30-motivational_game::v141-c-R006","30-motivational_game::v141-c-R005","30-motivational_game::v141-c-R002"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-189f5500ef3981fa","COMP-470db2b09bbdbdd2","COMP-4cf3718d101da7ca","COMP-80c9b12d3ea35c91","COMP-eeda8c162516d608"]});
